\ A recover consumes the error its own subtree raised, and nothing else. Its callers are still
\ live, so a later unrelated error in the same word renders the whole chain that reaches it.
\ Before the consumption bound, the capture cleared the live call stack too, and the `outer`
\ and `mid` rows below vanished from any error raised after a recover ran.
\
\ The `0 drop` tails keep each call non-tail, so no row is tail-elided. No flags, so the
\ interpreted and eager suites bind one golden.

quiet: ( -- ) [ [ f "caught here" caught: make-error throw ] [ drop ] recover ] ;
outer: ( -- ) [ quiet f "boom" late-error: make-error throw ] ;
mid:   ( -- ) [ outer 0 drop ] ;

mid 0 drop
